      "writtenOn": "2016-07-25T21:50:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this compilation check should be in one function, system level function say system_get_board_properties() or something - it is not necessarily only slave interface config.\n\nThat function should live in common/system.c, and that function should call board specific function based on conditional compilation.\n\nSo, the conditional compilation happens in one place only.\n\nWhen compiling for other boards you can remove zero, so that by default the interface is not enabled.\n\njust my 2c",
      "revId": "d7ca52a390780138f21a22646c7157116f3638a1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a6b739b_a87e4313",
        "filename": "chip/g/sps.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 242,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-07-25T23:12:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Added a function system_get_board_properties() in chip/g/system.c that can be called by sps_init and similarly i2cs_init() that returns a bit field. There is a unique bit for SPI and one for I2C options enabled. Therefore, the conditional compile has been removed from here. system_get_board_properties() returns 0 unless a board specific function is called.",
      "parentUuid": "4a6b739b_e2021cd8",
      "revId": "d7ca52a390780138f21a22646c7157116f3638a1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
